      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city sits on a salt dome, a geological feature that has shaped its landscape and even created sinkholes over the years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daisetta%2C_Texas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1981 a sinkhole grew from a smaller 1969 collapse, eventually forming a lake that now marks the town’s southern edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daisetta%2C_Texas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Daisetta was founded in 1918 after the nearby Hull oilfield was discovered, drawing planters and lumbermen who had been there since 1850.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/daisetta-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s salt dome not only influences topography but also sparked a 2008 sinkhole whose cause is still linked to oil drilling activity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
